.TH SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_NOTIFICATION_HEADER_ICON_STRING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_NOTIFICATION_HEADER_ICON_STRING \- The path to an image to be used as the header icon for system notifications on some platforms.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_notification.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_NOTIFICATION_HEADER_ICON_STRING \(dqSDL.notification.header_icon\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is required on: - Windows - *nix when not running in a container, and no \[char46]desktop entry is available
.PP
Image types supported depend on the platform, but \[char46]png generally offers the best compatability\[char46]
.PP
On *nix platforms, this can also be the name of a system icon, as specified by the Icon Naming Specification\[char46]
.PP
Can be set before calling
.BR SDL_ShowNotificationWithProperties ()
or
.BR SDL_ShowNotification ()
for the first time\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

